def modify_stairs(conn_header: ConnHeader, params: ModifyStairsParameters) -> dict:
    """
    Modifies Stair elements in place, keeping their baseline and position: the flight width, total height, number of
    steps, riser height and going with their locks, the top link to a story with its offset, the Rules and Standards
    (each limit and whether it is applied), the headroom (generation method, height and left and right offset; read
    back, and one Archicad did not apply is reported as an error), the finish and structure visibility, the extra top
    and bottom treads, the walking line position and offset, the step numbering, the walking direction, the uniform
    finish, monolith and draining settings, and for the flights and the landings the tread and riser settings (presence,
    thickness, offset, nosing, riser cross section and position) and the structure of each side (presence, type,
    underside shape and thickness, the monolith data of a Monolith structure: thinning, thickness, bottom oversize,
    building material and fill, surfaces, pens, line types and drainings, and the stringer data of a Side structure:
    width, height above tread and how it is measured; the monolith and stringer data are read back, and one Archicad did
    not apply is reported as an error), and the floor plan display: whether it is Custom or by the Model View Options,
    and for the floor plan and the reflected ceiling plan separately the stories the stair is shown on and whether its
    walking line, numbering, up/down text, description and structure are shown, the symbol on each story (above, top,
    middle, bottom and below the relevant stories), the break line (angle, gap and position) and the line type, pen and
    symbol fill overrides, and the line types, pens and fills of the structure symbols per structure type and view
    (structureSymbols) and of the monolithic structure per view and visible or hidden part (monolithStructureSymbols),
    and which structures, fills and monolithic parts are shown on each range of the relevant stories, per view
    (structureVisibilityOnStories); these are read back, and one Archicad did not apply is reported as an error.
    CreateStairs accepts the same settings. Only the given settings are changed. Archicad solves the stair again within
    its baseline, so it may adjust the step values; read them back with GetDetailsOfElements. A given going (treadDepth)
    is pinned in the Rules and Standards as CreateStairs pins it, before the given rules are written. Not written by
    this command: the baseline with its landings and winders; the subelements (treads, risers, structures) take the per-
    part settings above and cannot be written one by one through the API; the boundaries and the walking lines
    GetDetailsOfElements reads, which Archicad lays out itself from the baseline and the flight width and which the API
    cannot write (here, in CreateStairs and in RecreateStairs an item that gives one is refused with an error that says
    so).
    """
    return conn_header.core.post_tapir_command(
        command="ModifyStairs", parameters=params.model_dump(mode="json", by_alias=True, exclude_none=True)
    )


